  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool (config_005, 0.6501) is the clear best so far, and the RNA-only design space is well-mapped (avgpool > transformer, scvi > pca > scgpt, multi > single). Image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.208), but we have not tested a stronger image encoder. Uncertainty: whether a more powerful image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can provide complementary signal to the already-strong RNA representation. This experiment (config_036) tests the most logical multimodal extension: combining the best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with the strongest available image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) using simple concat fusion. It isolates the question 'does a strong image modality add value on top of the best RNA model?' with minimal confounding changes. With only 3 experiments remaining, this is the highest-upside test: if it beats 0.6501, we have a new best and can fine-tune fusion in the last 2 runs; if it does not, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and avoid wasting remaining budget on further image variants."
}

